From bea4015be7b847565c25474494ebe1cda843fafb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blue898 <201240079+blue898@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:49:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 143/146] ARM: dts: exynos4412-midas: write S-Boot's no-LPM
 marker where it reads it

S-Boot takes a restart for a restart only if INFORM2 holds 0x12345678.
INFORM2 is at offset 0x0808 of the PMU, not 0xF008, and the handler that
writes it had the default priority, the same as the SoC's own
syscon-reboot, which is registered first: the reset happened before the
marker was written.

So with a USB cable attached S-Boot took every reboot for "powered on by
the charger": it drew its battery screen over the logo and asked for the
charger mode (androidboot.mode=charger next to the device tree's
androidboot.mode=normal).

Use the right offset and a priority above the reset handler's. The price
is that handler's one second wait on every restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos4412-midas.dtsi | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos4412-midas.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos4412-midas.dtsi
index f1f0c6c68..7ae1ecbe4 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos4412-midas.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos4412-midas.dtsi
@@ -1109,8 +1109,13 @@ &pmu_system_controller {
 	assigned-clocks = <&pmu_system_controller 0>;
 	assigned-clock-parents = <&clock CLK_XUSBXTI>;
 
-	/* S-Boot 4.0 */
-	#define S5P_INFORM2		0xF008
+	/*
+	 * S-Boot 4.0. INFORM2 is at 0x0808: with 0x12345678 there S-Boot treats a
+	 * restart as a restart. Written to 0xF008 it never arrived, so with a USB
+	 * cable attached S-Boot took every reboot for "powered on by the charger",
+	 * drew its battery screen over the logo and asked for the charger mode.
+	 */
+	#define S5P_INFORM2		0x0808
 	#define S5P_INFORM3		0x080C
 	#define BOOT_MODE_PREFIX	0x12345670
 	#define BOOT_NORMAL		(BOOT_MODE_PREFIX | 0)
@@ -1121,6 +1126,12 @@ no-lpm-mode {
 		compatible = "syscon-reboot";
 		offset = <S5P_INFORM2>;
 		value = <0x12345678>;
+		/*
+		 * Before the SoC's own syscon-reboot (192, registered first), or
+		 * the reset happens and this is never written. The price is the
+		 * handler's one second wait on every restart.
+		 */
+		priority = <200>;
 	};
 
 	reboot-mode {
-- 
